id: pm-github-sync-setup-artifacts
title: Publish tracker sync after restoring workflow-owned setup artifacts
description: "Reusable sync setup can change merge attributes and the managed extension registry before its publication scope gate. Bound setup ownership to a clean baseline, remove only workflow-produced setup changes before the scope gate, preserve fail-closed rejection of caller edits, and verify nonempty import and repeat-import idempotency in synthetic callers."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: changelog-unreleased,"gh:unbraind/pm-github#168",sync,workflow
created_at: "2026-10-24T05:12:10.201Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T23:10:59.553Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T21:45:45.339Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-24T06:01:04.000Z"
author: codex-agent
resolution: Restores workflow-owned setup artifacts before tracker publication and proves only authorized tracker/changelog changes are published.
expected_result: "Reusable sync setup can change merge attributes and the managed extension registry before its publication scope gate. Bound setup ownership to a clean baseline, remove only workflow-produced setup changes before the scope gate, preserve fail-closed rejection of caller edits, and verify nonempty import and repeat-import idempotency in synthetic callers."
actual_result: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/173, merged 2026-10-24T06:01:04Z, merge f4c29e8391462d03be4c3303e8309ece7864c025: Restores workflow-owned setup artifacts before tracker publication and proves only authorized tracker/changelog changes are published."
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T05:12:14.891Z",codex-agent,"Issue #168 reviewed. Setup currently writes attributes and the managed-extension registry, but restoration covers only settings and workspace history and runs after the first scope gate. Plan: explicitly bound setup lifetime and restore only clean-baseline workflow artifacts before caller scripts and the publication gate; test absent/outdated attributes, tracked/untracked registries, nonempty plus identical repeat imports, and unrelated edits. Run targeted tests, typecheck and lint locally; use npm and Bun CI release gates for complete evidence."
  "2026-10-24T05:15:54.262Z",codex-agent,"Read all four hosted job logs through the jobs API: ADO, Gantt and Lint reject setup-written attributes; Slack rejects attributes plus the managed registry. The fix now brackets setup with a file-level clean check (index, working tree, and ignored untracked files) and immediate restoration before any import or caller script. Closeout shares the same vulnerable setup sequence, so it receives the identical boundary. Existing publication scope and privacy gates remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-24T05:21:34.822Z",codex-agent,"Regression-driven refinement: tracked registries also enter early privacy scans, while strict health requires managed-extension coverage and current attributes. Final design saves runtime setup outside the publication tree and immediately restores the clean checkout before all scans. Strict health temporarily reinstates those saved artifacts inside its own shell, with a baseline check before activation and an EXIT restoration trap on success or failure. The scope helper checks these two paths explicitly, including ignored files, both before setup and at every publication gate; caller edits are never discarded. No gate threshold, caller repository or dependency pin is changed."
  "2026-10-24T05:24:46.331Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: replaced only restore_workflow_setup_artifacts in the sync workflow with a no-op, leaving guards, workflow steps, importer and tests unchanged. Ran env GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 node --test --test-reporter=tap --test-name-pattern=\"setup artifacts never enter tracker publication: outdated attributes, untracked registry\" test/import-gate.test.ts. Reverted behaviour: 0 passed, 1 failed; after a nonempty import and identical repeat, the scope gate refused setup-written .gitattributes. Restored the function byte-for-byte and reran the exact command: 1 passed, 0 failed."
  "2026-10-24T05:24:47.685Z",codex-agent,"Local evidence: 20 distinct targeted tests passed: setup publication and caller refusal/ordering 10, health failure cleanup and publication safety 4, literal scope operands 4, and closeout contract plus real repeat publication 2. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and npm run lint passed. pm test --run --progress passed all 4 linked commands, including the four setup-publication variants. Test-result tracking is disabled by project policy, so pass evidence is recorded here without changing that policy. Full npm and Bun release gates will run in CI because the shared host is saturated."
  "2026-10-24T05:25:36.320Z",codex-agent,"Pre-push changelog generation and changelog:check passed. Strict project health passed with a scratch global-extension root. The normal host health invocation reports a global-extension host-version skew between the repo-pinned host and the newer ambient host; no dependency pin or global configuration was changed. The item remains in_progress and is released for orchestrator verification."
